WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.362
Where are agencies?

2
00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:04.613
The workbook's baseline is G C C Moderate.

3
00:00:04.613 --> 00:00:07.947
Microsoft 365 G C C pairs
with commercial Azure,

4
00:00:07.947 --> 00:00:11.880
so a G C C agency's subscriptions
are usually commercial,

5
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:16.924
and the guide's commands run as written,
with the cloud set to Azure Cloud.

6
00:00:16.924 --> 00:00:21.038
Azure Government is a side note: it
pairs with G C C High and D O D.

7
00:00:21.038 --> 00:00:25.809
Learn's page, Compare Azure Government
and global Azure, says a service

8
00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:30.663
available there has all its features
unless the page lists a variation.

9
00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:34.739
The differences that matter for
this module: the endpoints differ,

10
00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:38.667
with Resource Manager at management
dot U S gov cloud A P I dot net;

11
00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:42.372
the landing zone accelerators
aren't supported unmodified,

12
00:00:42.372 --> 00:00:45.781
so the code has to be adapted;
and Azure Lighthouse has no

13
00:00:45.781 --> 00:00:49.338
pim for delegated access and
no delegation across clouds.

14
00:00:49.338 --> 00:00:52.320
Later modules name the
gaps for their own steps.
